        "contract": {
            "acceptance_criteria": [
                "A voice report (failure or end) of an earlier tile tap changes nothing; a newer tap's state is kept (tested)",
                "When a tile's voice fails while the view is paused, the keyboard focus stays on that tile (tested)",
                "With no tile taken, idle closes the view instead of pausing; idle also fires when every frame fails conversion (tested)",
                "A hidden page noticed first through a frame pauses with the tiles like the visibilitychange handler; a hidden board region still closes to idle (tested, the region case asserts idle)",
                "Voice trouble counts carry across a camera switch (tested, documented)",
                "Caregiver demo view: the stored-clip error line is a live region filled after insertion; a second unplayable recording in a row says this browser cannot play clips and suggests another browser; the bounded wait after 'Aufnahme beenden' covers the conversion too (tested)",
                "attachRecognise declares pressedAt before the demo code that consumes it"
            ],
            "goal": "Close the code-level review notes of the continuous gesture view (NG-57) and of Vormachen (NG-61): stale voice reports ignored, tile focus kept, idle and page-hide edge cases, and clearer clip failure handling in the caregiver area.",
